:" One step of a PID controller with clamped output and integrator.

   A reference program of the static profile (docs/static-profile.md). The
   target provides two functions, read_adc(channel) and write_pwm(channel;duty)
   in C, which board.kg declares and exports as board.adc and board.pwm. Under
   KlongPy they are Python functions bound by C symbol before the file is loaded
   (see board.kg).

   Check it:   kgpy check examples/embedded/pid.kg
   Expected:   examples/embedded/pid.expect
"

kp::2.0
ki::0.5
kd::0.1
dt::0.01
lo::0.0
hi::1.0

integ::0.0
prev::0.0

.l("board")

clamp::{(x|lo)&hi}

step::{[e u];e::x-board.adc(0);integ::clamp(integ+ki*e*dt);u::clamp((kp*e)+integ+kd*(e-prev)%dt);prev::e;board.pwm(0;u);u}

.entry("step";"float -> float")
